BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Nectar Feeders vs. Insect Hunters: A Closer Look at Bats
DTSTART;TZID=America/Chicago:20260624T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Chicago:20260624T130000
DTSTAMP:20260601T133821Z
UID:00ed435a7aa38fe3cc540bed882013aa@family-events-agent
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:museum,science,family,all_audiences
DESCRIPTION:Organizer: Field Museum - Events\\nCost: Included with admissi
 on\\nAges: All ages\\nCategory: General\\n\\nCelebrate Pollinator Week wit
 h scientists from the Gantz Family Collections Center! Bats are often cele
 brated as important nighttime pollinators\, but not all bats play that rol
 e. At this special session\, you’ll learn about the fascinating diversit
 y of bat diets and adaptations around the globe. Even though Chicagoland
 ’s bats do not pollinate our local flowers\, they do rely on insect poll
 inators as part of their diets. Stop by the Grainger Science Hub to learn 
 more and to see a live dissection of our local bat species\, and special s
 pecimens of pollinating bats from around the world\, too. Guests will lear
 n the diversity of bats and be able to recall how our local bats are not p
 ollinators\, but they are still an important part of our local ecosystem. 
 Presenters include Lauren Johnson\, Assistant Collections Manager\, Mammal
 s. Please note: this session will feature a live dissection.\\n\\nMore inf
 o: https://www.fieldmuseum.org/our-events/meet-a-scientist/nectar-feeders-
 vs-insect-hunters-a-closer-look-at-bats
LOCATION:Field Museum\, 1400 S Lake Shore Dr\, Chicago\, IL 60605
URL:https://www.fieldmuseum.org/our-events/meet-a-scientist/nectar-feeders
 -vs-insect-hunters-a-closer-look-at-bats
BEGIN:VALARM
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:Tomorrow: Nectar Feeders vs. Insect Hunters: A Closer Look at 
 Bats
TRIGGER:-P1D
END:VALARM
BEGIN:VALARM
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:In 2 hours: Nectar Feeders vs. Insect Hunters: A Closer Look a
 t Bats
TRIGGER:-PT2H
END:VALARM
END:VEVENT
